/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  Knock-out drum at 30 bar: removes ~86 % of the water formed in the deoxo.

  This is the ONLY unit in the plant that ever holds a liquid phase which is
  not ammonia: the condensate here is essentially pure WATER, the water the
  deoxo made out of the oxygen the industrial nitrogen brought in.

  That is why this whole sector carries its OWN property package, in
  PURIFICATION/constant/thermoPhysPropDict -- water as the solvent instead of
  ammonia.  Read that file: it is the clearest example in the case of why
  `constant/` exists at every level of a fractal plant.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
type      isothermalFlash;
operation { P 30 bar; }
boundary  { inlets ( Feed );  outlets ( Liquid  Vapour ); }
